WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.400
What can you tell us about overcoming

00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:06.080
doubt when pursuing like your own path

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:10.160
to success?

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:11.920
>> I'll tell you that I know a lot of

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.160
incompetent I don't know if incompetent

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.880
is the right word, but I I know a lot of

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.039
normal people who make an abnormal

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.520
amount of money just because they're not

00:00:19.039 --> 00:00:24.640
insecure.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:26.640
I think one of my gifts from a very

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.400
young age is a and it's also a little

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:30.800
bit of a curse. there's a balance here

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.680
is just an unwavering irrational

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.120
confidence almost. Um, hey, I can do it.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.120
Nobody has to give me permission. I can

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.239
do this. Um, I know it's going to be

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:39.520
scary. I know it's going to be hard. I

00:00:38.239 --> 00:00:41.280
think part of it comes from the fact

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.160
that I'm an optimist. So, I think that

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.760
everything is going to be a little bit

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:45.440
easier than it's going to be that it

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.559
ends up being. Um, everybody in business

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:51.120
knows that story. But, yeah, man. Like,

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:52.960
life is hard. Business is hard. Um,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:55.600
doing anything at a high level is really

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.800
hard. So, you might as well just get

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:58.800
comfortable in these uncomfortable

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:01.440
situations and treat it like a muscle

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:02.800
and uh work it out and just practice

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.559
being in these uncomfortable situations.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.080
And I've been kind of doing that my

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:08.080
entire career from yeah, buying that

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.439
first cargo van on Craigslist and

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.159
getting made fun of for starting that

00:01:09.439 --> 00:01:13.600
moving company. Um to man, yeah, you're

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:14.799
you're writing a book and you get a big

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:18.400
book deal and then you're in your own

00:01:14.799 --> 00:01:20.080
head for six months working on it and

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:22.320
you got no feedback. I'm used to a world

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.640
where I can tweet and seconds later I

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.640
have positive or negative feedback from

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.799
thousands of people and yeah, you write

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.200
a you write a whole book with without

00:01:28.799 --> 00:01:33.439
that external feedback. So yeah, there's

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:34.400
there's there's highs where I think this

00:01:33.439 --> 00:01:35.520
is going to be awesome and it's going to

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.200
sell a bunch of copies and then there's

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.520
lows where I'm like, man, I didn't have

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.040
permission to write this. Like who am I?

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:45.119
Mhm. Now, you said that you said that

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.320
you maybe felt that way like even as a

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:50.079
kid for those who don't necessarily just

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.799
aren't aren't born that way. Is there a

00:01:50.079 --> 00:01:55.520
way to build that muscle?

00:01:52.799 --> 00:01:57.200
Yeah. I like I like literally writing

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.040
down the worst thing that can happen

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:01.280
when you're about to make a a career

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.280
defining decision.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.280
So, it it it's called fear setting. It

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.040
was popularized by Tim Ferrris. My style

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.399
is a little bit different, but when I'm

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:10.560
about to make a decision, whether it's

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:12.879
hiring somebody, buying a building,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.239
buying a company, building a building

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:15.680
that first self- storage facility,

00:02:14.239 --> 00:02:18.800
launching in a new market, whatever it

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.480
might be, my question and my process is

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.640
always the same. Like, okay, wake up

00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:25.280
early, get coffee, get a blank piece of

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:28.800
paper, and literally write down the

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:30.400
worst case scenario. If the worst string

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.040
of events happens after you make this

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:36.400
decision, write it down like what

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.239
happened first. Okay? Like this branch

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.400
didn't work, we lost 50 grand or this

00:02:38.239 --> 00:02:41.680
building didn't work. The worst case

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:43.599
scenario on that first building, I

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.879
personally guaranteed $1.5 million of

00:02:43.599 --> 00:02:46.959
debt to build that first self- storage

00:02:44.879 --> 00:02:49.840
facility. Worst thing scenario there was

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:51.360
literal bankruptcy. I lose my business.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:52.879
Didn't have a house yet, so and I didn't

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.080
have any kids yet, so it was a little

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:55.599
bit easier to swallow than it would be

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.360
for a lot of people.

00:02:55.599 --> 00:02:59.920
I wrote it all down. It's like

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:01.840
bankruptcy. Okay, then what? What does

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:03.920
my life actually look like if I go

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.599
bankrupt? Well, I'm not in China where I

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.879
have a personal credit score and I can

00:03:05.599 --> 00:03:08.640
never get a loan again for the rest of

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:11.040
my life and actually can't even get a

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.599
job. I'm in America where bankruptcy is

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:15.280
temporary. I have two parents who are

00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:16.640
still married and they have a house and

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.040
while it's a small house, I could

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:20.879
probably take my wife and my newborn

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.519
that was on the way. Take them there and

00:03:20.879 --> 00:03:24.879
and you know, live in that basement and

00:03:23.519 --> 00:03:26.159
I could get another job at a real estate

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:27.840
business because we built a self-

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:29.440
storage facility. I could probably go

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:32.640
make 200 grand a year because of what I

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:34.640
learned. That's not so bad.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:37.040
>> Mhm.

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:38.640
So, is it is it a matter of becoming

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.080
comfortable with the worst case scenario

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.400
or is there something to be said about

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.560
limiting that downside risk?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.840
>> Absolutely. There's absolutely it's a

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.440
combination and this is a balance,

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:49.360
right? I'm not telling people to get out

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:52.080
there and just be be dangerous, but I

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:53.760
think just seeing it on paper, like

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:56.400
looking at it and thinking about

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.760
yourself in that situation, all of a

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:02.080
sudden it's not as daunting as you

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:05.680
thought. And very few decisions or

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:07.200
career changes or new ventures can even

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:08.480
even have the potential to bankrupt you

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.720
if you treat them the right way. If you

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.200
bootstrap them, if you do whatever. So,

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.599
um yeah, many times I fear set like I'm

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:17.359
about to walk into a meeting with a with

00:04:15.599 --> 00:04:18.479
a a really good friend of mine. This was

00:04:17.359 --> 00:04:20.320
one of the hardest conversations I've

00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:22.000
ever had. He stood up at my wedding and

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:23.680
about a month later I needed to like

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.400
fire him from my company. He worked for

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:28.080
me right before I was just super anxious

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.880
about this all week. I wasn't sleeping.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.160
It was just a a gut-wrenchingish

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:33.280
problem and it wasn't even all him. It

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.560
was like our business couldn't support

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:37.919
him in one area. And so I did fear

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:39.440
setting before that conversation like,

00:04:37.919 --> 00:04:43.120
"Hey, what's the worst thing that can

00:04:39.440 --> 00:04:45.199
happen here?" Nick says something

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:47.840
rude and mean that he can't take back

00:04:45.199 --> 00:04:51.040
and it ruins the relationship.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.320
Okay, saw it on paper. We know this

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.080
guy's gonna go get another job. He's

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:56.320
very wellworked. He's got a supportive

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:58.080
family.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:05:00.160
The worst case scenario is like I can

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:02.320
control that. A circle is like I can

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:04.720
control that. Keep your cool. Don't say

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:06.240
anything stupid. Treat the guy with

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.720
empathy.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.560
And it was fine. I felt better after the

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:13.600
meeting. So yeah, it's a it's a

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:13.600
combination for

